= Future directions

== Checking the construction and exploring order two

*Verify the proposed counterexample.* The proof for $L_4 h=h'''$ on slide 1.5
was generated by AI. A human review should check that the construction gives
a smooth $f$ and that $f^((3n))$ converges at every point of the exceptional set.

*What happens at order two?* Let $I$ be an open interval and $f,a_0,a_1,a_2 in C^oo (I)$, with
$a_2 (x)!=0$ for every $x in I$. Define
$
  (L h)(x)=a_2 (x) h''(x)+a_1 (x) h'(x)+a_0 (x) h(x).
$

If $L^n f -> g$ pointwise on $I$, must $g$ be smooth
and satisfy $L g=g$?
